e":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only one-pixel-per-point modes of exactly the target size qualify, so a HiDPI “looks like"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1920x1080” mode on a 4K timing is never chosen. Interlaced and stretched modes and modes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"macOS does not offer for the desktop are skipped. Of the rest, the rate nearest the target"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wins: exact 60.00 beats 59.94 for a 60 Hz target, and 59.94 beats 60.00 for a 59.94 one."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A rate more than half a hertz off does not qualify, so 120 Hz never stands in for 60. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mode reporting no rate qualifies only when no mode reports one. Ties go to the lower mode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ID, so the answer does not depend on list order."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/ModeSelection\/choose(for:among:current:)"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwiremackit\/modeselection\/choose(for:among:current:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Type Method","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"choose"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"for"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14HeadwireMacKit10ModeTargetV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ModeTarget"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"among"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14HeadwireMacKit17DisplayModeOptionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DisplayModeOption"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"current"},{"